    "result_text": "That's just JaCoCo coverage excludes. The `BUILD SUCCESS` with the acceptance test passing confirms the implementation works.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a new `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the script-initialized schema; I updated all four dialects for consistency.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the build-time generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n4. **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 assigns the code right before saving, via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (handles names shorter than 3).\n   - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits \u2014 a global sequence one more than the current owner count.\n\n**Verification:** The acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (the only test in the suite) passes \u2014 it confirms codes start with `SMI-`/`JON-` and that the global sequence increments by exactly one between consecutive creates. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
